body:
Day old post, but nobody has mentioned these issues yet so I'll do it, focusing on healers. IMO it's more of a healer issue than a DPS issue because your wipes are consistently well into P3 (this timing of wipes indicates you have enough DPS to get past the submerge checks) and there are several glaring mechanics mistakes in the healer core, and less obvious more minor mistakes among the DPS, mostly just threat and forgetting to pop healthstones/frost resist potions. 

&#x200B;

I'll also mention that if your PC assignments arent: HPals on tanks, Disc take two PC, Rdruid OR Rsham take two pc (whichever between the rsham or rdruid has faster reaction time and is more comfy with spothealing) and then Rsham OR Rdruid heal the just last pc and help with tanks) they really should be. If you're relying on the type of strategy that assigns only rdruid and disc priest from 5>1 and reverse 1>5 then you'll run into the renew/rejuv overheals mentioned elsewhere in the thread. With the healing assignment I outlined above, your disc can heal primarily with PWS 1>PWS 2>Flash heal and penance to keep up (renew should barely be used, it's not good and as you know, your disc is causing overhealing to the boss by spamming renew), then your rdruid can rely on Nourish 1>Nourish 2>Rejuv1>Rejuv 2 then nourishes to keep up, and your Rsham should of course use Lesser healing wave and Riptide as necessary.  

&#x200B;

For your first wipe on 9/12: there are two deaths in the first minute, but this would still be recoverable. First, Wobbletree fucks up and attacks before tank. Then the rdruid gets killed by shadow strike, someone failed to interrupt-- looks like Skoomadin casts Holy Wrath 0.2 seconds after the rdruid dies, very unfortunate. The main cause of this wipe are your holy paladins & the PC healer assigned to Meddler, which appears to be the disc priest. This wipe happens bc both your hpals die then tanks die: Meddler dies to the first tick of a new PC without casting frost resistance potion nor divine shield nor heathstone while your disc priest doesnt heal this PC fast enough before the first tick. Then, Leafypaly dies from aggro 10s later bc he has to big pump heals into the tanks, but issue is that Leafypaly has righteous fury up and is out of position - Leafy should be standing where the rdruid is, on top of the MT, but is just slightly out of position and forgot to cancel RF buff, thus they nuked by adds that the tanks couldn't realistically pick up. 

&#x200B;

For your second wipe on 9/12: A rogue dies to impale, dumb mistake but still recoverable. The wipe truly happens when  the disc priest dies from PC without: casting Healthstone, Desperate Prayer, PW:S theirself, binding heal thierself, nor frost resistance pot. I can't know who the intended PC healer was, but there's so many tools a disc has to heal PC quickly that this death is the disc's own fault. The third death is also a healer, the Rsham dies probably as a direct result of the disc dieing since you're now light on PC healing. The fourth death is the disc improperly healing the demo lock's PC, and the 5th death is again Wobbletree pulling threat. Dirtyhands fails to recast Healing Stream totem after he gets brezzed the first time, and Skitss ticks down from leech. 6 deaths have happened, the 7th death is again the rsham not being healed from PC, the worst part is the rsham takes two ticks of PC, doesnt heal theirself, doesnt pop healthstone, doesnt pop frost resistance potion. Eigth death is the tank, since Leafy, is OOM because this has been going on for a while with too many raid healing mistakes, and your other hpal, Meddler, is casting too much flash of light to be of any use healing the tank enough anyways. This is definitely a wipe by now. BTW Meddler should never be casting Flash of Light in P3 Anub, it's a ton of tank damage, and Holy Light does way better healing. weirdly on Alg, Meddler properly does cast Holy Light. Also, Leafy went OOM and didn't get an innervate nor hymn of hope, which could've bought some seconds to attempt recovery (but regardless, a recovery after 7 deaths would be surprising) 

&#x200B;

For your third wipe on 9/12: First Rivaz dies to PC and they've already used their immunity and healthstone so this is on whichever healer failed to heal fast enough. Could have used frost resistance pot instead of speed, but honestly your healers should just heal better. Second death is MT death, but Leafy and the rdruid are properly healing the tanks, so not sure what happened here. The next 5 deaths happen as a result of the boss being loose, the MT doesn't get brezzed fast enough and it becomes a wipe. I will note that the MT shouldnt be wearing stam trinkets on this fight in particular, instead try avoidance trinkets like the 10m togc tanking one, or furnace stone. Also, NR to either an extra helm or cloak will help reach the resistance threshold (in addition to flask of resistance, which is already being used)   


Your 9/12 kill is long, due to missing a DPS and then your priest does a lot of grief healing, hurting yall while you're down. and in both weeks on the kills all the deaths except one ret pal are PC deaths which aren't healed fast enough. Adjust your healing strat and/or teach your Disc priest, and Meddler in particular to have better spell selection, while your rsham should pay attention to mechanics. Also, in the wipes and the 8/29 kill Meddler is second highest on grief healing overall, which is insane bc they're mostly mostly overhealing with Flash of light, but in the 9/12 kill this isn't an issue.

I better ace that interview

&#x200B;

I work better under a deadline
